<block-guide name="core/tab-list"><![CDATA[
CORE/TAB-LIST
The row of tab buttons; first child of core/tabs. Full guide and example: see core/tabs.

MARKUP
<!-- wp:tab-list -->
<div role="tablist" class="wp-block-tab-list"><button type="button" role="tab">Overview</button><button type="button" role="tab">Pricing</button></div>
<!-- /wp:tab-list -->
No inner blocks: one <button type="button" role="tab"> per tab, in panel order, on one line.
Each button's text must equal the "label" of the core/tab-panel at the same position.

STYLING
Colour and border set on this block are written on EVERY <button> (class and inline style),
not on the div. ariaLabel names the tab row for screen readers (default "Tabbed content").
]]></block-guide>
